  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Key findings for the plan:\n\n- **webpack** declares `@babel/core`/`@babel/preset-react`/`babel-loader` only under `devDependencies` in `package.json` (used for its own test fixtures/examples). Webpack's own module parsing uses `acorn`, not Babel \u2014 it is not reached by a Babel parser AST change.\n- **next.js** (`packages/next/package.json`) declares `@babel/core`, `@babel/traverse`, `@babel/generator`, `@babel/types`, `@babel/preset-*`, etc. also under `devDependencies`, but these are bundled at build time and power Next's real `babel-loader`/custom `.babelrc` transform pipeline used at runtime for user code \u2014 this is the actual consuming edge for a Babel parser AST change.\n- **babel** itself is the origin of the change.\n\nPlan: Babel (origin) \u2192 next.js (real consumer via its babel-loader compilation path) \u2192 webpack unaffected (parses with acorn, no propagation needed; its Babel devDependency is test-only tooling).",
